<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>DeficitLens verified Apple Watch report</title>
  <style>
    :root { --ink:#18202a; --muted:#5d6875; --blue:#4c78a8; --red:#e45756; --paper:#fff; --wash:#f4f7fa; }
    * { box-sizing:border-box; }
    body { margin:0; color:var(--ink); background:var(--wash); font:15px/1.55 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",sans-serif; }
    header { padding:56px max(24px,calc((100vw - 1120px)/2)); background:#122334; color:white; }
    header p { max-width:760px; color:#d9e4ee; }
    main { max-width:1120px; margin:0 auto; padding:30px 24px 70px; }
    section { background:var(--paper); padding:26px; margin:18px 0; border-radius:14px; box-shadow:0 3px 16px #19324a12; }
    h1,h2,h3 { line-height:1.2; }
    h1 { margin:0; font-size:42px; }
    h2 { margin-top:0; }
    .cards { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(190px,1fr)); gap:14px; }
    .card { padding:18px; border:1px solid #dce4eb; border-radius:10px; }
    .number { display:block; color:var(--blue); font-size:29px; font-weight:750; }
    .label { color:var(--muted); }
    img { display:block; width:100%; height:auto; margin:18px auto; }
    .table-wrap { overflow-x:auto; }
    .data-table { border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; font-size:13px; }
    .data-table th,.data-table td { padding:8px 10px; border-bottom:1px solid #e3e8ed; text-align:right; white-space:nowrap; }
    .data-table th:first-child,.data-table td:first-child { text-align:left; }
    .warning { border-left:5px solid var(--red); background:#fff5f4; padding:14px 18px; }
    code { background:#edf1f5; padding:2px 5px; border-radius:4px; }
    footer { color:var(--muted); text-align:center; padding-top:28px; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<header>
  <h1>DeficitLens</h1>
  <p>A leakage-safe Apple Watch energy-expenditure audit: criterion oxygen uptake, nested participant-level validation, conformal uncertainty, subgroup slices, and explicit fat-loss planning scenarios.</p>
</header>
<main>
  <section>
    <h2>Executive result</h2>
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card"><span class="number">{{ evidence.weee.participants }}</span><span class="label">WEEE participants held out once each</span></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="number">{{ evidence.weee.rows }}</span><span class="label">non-overlapping 30-second windows</span></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="number">{{ high_resolution_rows }}</span><span class="label">5-second-stride sensitivity windows</span></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="number">{{ "%.1f"|format(ensemble_improvement_pct) }}%</span><span class="label">ensemble MAE change vs raw Apple</span></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="number">{{ "%.1f"|format(interval.coverage * 100) }}%</span><span class="label">cluster-robust coverage (90% target)</span></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="number">{{ external_primary.participants }}</span><span class="label">independent Series 8 paired sessions</span></div>
    </div>
    <p>The best point estimator by held-out-participant MAE was <strong>{{ best.model }}</strong>. A more complex model is retained only when out-of-fold stacking assigns it weight.</p>
    <div class="warning"><strong>Interpretation boundary:</strong> these are exercise-energy measurement audits, not a guarantee of individual calorie burn or a weight-loss prediction.</div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Model comparison</h2>
    <img src="figures/model_error.png" alt="MAE and mean bias for all models">
    <div class="table-wrap">{{ metrics_table | safe }}</div>
    <h3>Participant-clustered 95% intervals</h3>
    <div class="table-wrap">{{ bootstrap_table | safe }}</div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Held-out predictions and calibrated uncertainty</h2>
    <img src="figures/observed_predicted.png" alt="Observed versus predicted active energy">
    <img src="figures/coverage_by_activity.png" alt="Conformal coverage by activity">
    <p>The outer test participant is absent from model fitting, stacking-weight learning, and conformal calibration. Calibration participants are also absent from base-model fitting. The primary interval calibrates participant-level maximum residuals; the more compact window-level interval covered {{ "%.1f"|format(compact_interval.coverage * 100) }}% and is retained as a diagnostic, not promoted as the primary interval.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Independent Apple Watch Series 8 audit</h2>
    <img src="figures/external_agreement.png" alt="Apple Watch versus COSMED K5 agreement">
    <p>Primary paired analysis: MAE <strong>{{ "%.2f"|format(external_primary.mae) }} kcal</strong>, mean bias <strong>{{ "%.2f"|format(external_primary.mean_bias) }} kcal</strong>, MAPE <strong>{{ "%.1f"|format(external_primary.mape) }}%</strong>. The all-paired sensitivity analysis, which restores the paper-wide excluded participant, has MAE {{ "%.2f"|format(external_all.mae) }} kcal.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap">{{ external_subgroup_table | safe }}</div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Subgroup audit</h2>
    <p>Cells with fewer than three participants are marked low-support and must not be read as stable fairness estimates. Activity slices contain repeated windows and are descriptive.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap">{{ subgroup_table | safe }}</div>
    <h3>Supported-cell disparities</h3>
    <div class="table-wrap">{{ disparity_table | safe }}</div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Fat-loss planning impact</h2>
    <p>This table asks a narrow counterfactual: if the participant-level mean rate error across cycling/running windows repeated for 30, 45, or 60 exercise minutes daily, what fixed 7,700 kcal/kg arithmetic difference would accumulate? Sit/stand windows are excluded. It does not model metabolic adaptation, intake error, water, or behavior.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap">{{ decision_table | safe }}</div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Data and reproducibility</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>WEEE: {{ evidence.weee.checksum }}, Apple Watch Series 6, VO₂ criterion approximation, six protocol activities.</li>
      <li>External PAEE 2026: {{ evidence.apple_watch_paee_2026.checksum }}, Apple Watch Series 8 versus COSMED K5.</li>
      <li>Known timestamp anomaly: {{ evidence.weee.notes | join('; ') }}.</li>
      <li>Runtime: {{ "%.1f"|format(elapsed_seconds) }} seconds; DeficitLens {{ version }}; deterministic seed recorded in <code>run_manifest.json</code>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <footer>Generated {{ generated_at }} · See the repository model card and validation protocol before reuse.</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
